cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this work, please cite it as below.
title: >-
  waveguide-pixel-array: a coupled-waveguide pixel array for near-field image
  encoding
authors:
  - family-names: Chan
    given-names: King Ho
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0009-0002-0435-2030
    affiliation: Department of Physics, The Hong Kong University of Science and Technology, Hong Kong
type: software
license: MIT
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24435613
repository-code: https://github.com/55093693k-dot/waveguide-pixel-array
abstract: >-
  A binary image is written into a photonic chip as the transverse position of
  guided light in a pair of coupled waveguides, and read back by imaging the near
  field above the chip. All 400 pixels of a 20 by 20 image and all 441 pixels of a
  21 by 21 image read out correctly with a single threshold.
keywords:
  - silicon photonics
  - near-field imaging
  - image encoding
  - coupled waveguides

